<KickdriveProject>
 <module label="Project Home" panelVisible="1" type="project">
  <docs>
   <default>
    <html>
     <head>
      <meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1">
       <title>MovingCap Ethernet Drives</title>
      </meta>
      <link href="template.css" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css"/>
     </head>
     <body>
      <h1>MovingCap flatTRACK Testing Example</h1>
      <p>This known-working Kickdrive project is a blueprint for setup, service, parameter configuration, and motion testing of a MovingCap flatTRACK or shortTRACK Ethernet drive. It combines Ethernet communication, drive setup, an object editor, scope and trigger views, reusable parameter sets, and the embedded <strong>flattrack_demo.py</strong> MovingCap CODE application.</p>
      <p>The saved project contains values captured from the system on which it was prepared, including parameter readouts, timestamps, plot state, and user-interface state. Treat these as an illustrative project snapshot, not as prescribed settings. Before connecting or writing parameters, verify the drive IP address, node ID, matching XDD file, soft limits, controller gains, payload data, current limits, and every motion parameter for the target mechanics.</p>
      <p><strong>Safety:</strong> Starting the embedded script enables the drive and moves the axis automatically and continuously. The script intentionally waits without a timeout for target reached and fault clearance. This is diagnostic behavior: if a move does not complete, inspect the drive status, active fault, mechanics, and configuration rather than expecting an automatic recovery.</p>
      <h2>How to use this project</h2>
      <ul>
       <li>Connect the PC and MovingCap Ethernet drive to the same network.</li>
       <li>Make sure the drive and PC are in the same IP subnet.<br/>&#xd;
	   The default MovingCap IPv4 address is <strong>192.168.2.150</strong>. For example, configure the PC network interface as 192.168.2.10 with prefix length 24 (subnet mask 255.255.255.0).</li>
       <li>Open the <a href="#app:panel,Communication">Communication</a> module and check if the IP address is the same as your MovingCap Ethernet drive.<br/>&#xd;
	   Tip: The MovingCap Ethernet status LED uses Morse code to indicate the current IP address. A Morse-code app can help decode the blinking LED.&#xd;
	   </li>
       <li>Switch on the drive power supply and confirm that the axis can move safely.</li>
       <li>Open <a href="#app:panel,MC Eth Drive - Setup">MC Eth Drive - Setup</a> to identify and commission the drive. Do not start motion until the project settings have been checked.</li>
       <li>Use <a href="#app:panel,MC Eth Drive - Object Editor">MC Eth Drive - Object Editor</a> to inspect or modify selected CiA 402 and MovingCap parameters.</li>
       <li>Review the parameter-set modules before reading from or writing to the drive. Their values are examples for the original flatTRACK test system and may not suit another motor or mechanism.</li>
       <li>Open <a href="#app:panel,Scope">Scope</a>, drag one or more parameters from the Object Editor to the Scope &#xd;
	   area, and press 'Start' to sample. Double-click a parameter to create a plot.&#xd;
	   	<br/>&#xd;
	    Use the 'Record' button to store sampled data in a file. By default, the file is stored with the %%AppTitle%% project data. Use 'Open' in the Scope toolbar to load a recording, and use 'Save Project' in the main toolbar to store the relevant data in a '.kickzip' project file.	   &#xd;&#xd;&#xd;&#xd;&#xd;&#xd;
	   <br/>&#xd;
	   Use <a href="#app:panel,Scope - Trigger">Scope - Trigger</a> to define trigger conditions and record measurements immediately before and &#xd;&#xd;&#xd;&#xd;&#xd;&#xd;
	   after a trigger event. &#xd;
	   </li>
      </ul>
     </body>
    </html>
   </default>
  </docs>
  <module label="Communication" description="Allows CAN-style communication via TCP or CAN bus" panelVisible="0" type="canusb">
   <module label="CAN Monitor" panelVisible="0" type="canmonitor"/>
   <properties>
    <Port>net:192.168.2.150:15001</Port>
    <Baudrate>250K</Baudrate>
    <DebugMode>0</DebugMode>
    <MonitorFilter0>id = 81-ff # emergency msg only</MonitorFilter0>
    <MonitorFilter1>id != 81-ff # hide emergency msg</MonitorFilter1>
    <MonitorFilter2>dir = tx # tx data only</MonitorFilter2>
    <MonitorFilter3>exclude index = 6063, index = 606c # hide pos/velocity readout</MonitorFilter3>
    <MonitorFilter4>index = 6041 # show drive status only</MonitorFilter4>
    <MonitorFilter5>data = 80 * # show SDO abort transfer / error codes</MonitorFilter5>
   </properties>
  </module>
  <module userLevel="1" label="Scope" description="Scope / Data Logger" panelVisible="0" dragDropMode="1" type="datalog">
   <module label="Trigger" panelVisible="0" type="trigger"/>
   <docs>
    <DisplayedKickPlots>
     <Containers/>
    </DisplayedKickPlots>
    <MonitoringObjects>
     <CANopenObjectList>
      <CANopenObject index="6064" name="pos[mm]" nodeId="50" kickScaling="0.001" actualValue="43005" dataType="0004" objectType="7" uniqueIDRef="UID_PARAM_6064" PDOmapping="TPDO" monitorInterval="2" kickUiFormat="updates:r200; shape:slider; range:-32768,32768; step:1"/>
      <CANopenObject accessType="ro" index="60F4" name="ferr" nodeId="50" actualValue="5" dataType="0004" objectType="7" uniqueIDRef="UID_PARAM_60f4" PDOmapping="no" monitorInterval="2" kickUiFormat="updates:r1000; shape:slider; range:-2.14748e+09,2.14748e+09; step:5000"/>
     </CANopenObjectList>
    </MonitoringObjects>
   </docs>
   <properties>
    <TriggerConfig>050.60F4h.00h &lt; 50;050.60F4h.00h > -50</TriggerConfig>
    <PreTriggerTimeMsec>100</PreTriggerTimeMsec>
    <PostTriggerTimeMsec>200</PostTriggerTimeMsec>
    <TriggerState>1</TriggerState>
   </properties>
   <module userLevel="1" label="Pos-Err" description="Scope Panel" panelVisible="0" type="datalog_plot">
    <docs>
     <PlotConfigurationDoc>
      <PlotConfiguration xScale="200 msec/div" yScale="a" title="Pos-Err" cursorPosition="10">
       <Curves>
        <CurveConfiguration colorName="#000080" objectName="050.6064h.00h pos[mm]" dataObjectId="050.6064h.00h"/>
        <CurveConfiguration colorName="#800000" objectName="050.60f4h.00h ferr" dataObjectId="050.60f4h.00h"/>
       </Curves>
      </PlotConfiguration>
     </PlotConfigurationDoc>
    </docs>
   </module>
   <slave label="Communication" type="canusb"/>
  </module>
  <module label="MC Eth Drive" description="MovingCap Ethernet Drive" panelVisible="0" type="drive_vdc">
   <module userLevel="1" label="Setup" description="Initial Setup and Test" panelVisible="0" type="drive_canopen_setup"/>
   <module userLevel="1" label="Object Editor" description="Read/Edit/Write Drive Parameters" panelVisible="0" type="drive_canopen_objects">
    <docs>
     <EditorObjects>
      <CANopenObjectList>
       <CANopenObject accessType="ro" kickStatusTxt="15:42:25 read ok" index="6064" name="Position actual value" nodeId="50" actualValue="33214" defaultValue="0" dataType="0004" kickStatus="1" objectType="7" uniqueIDRef="UID_PARAM_6064" PDOmapping="TPDO" kickUiFormat="updates:r1000; shape:slider; range:-2.14748e+09,2.14748e+09; step:5000"/>
       <CANopenObject accessType="ro" kickStatusTxt="15:42:25 read ok" index="606C" name="Velocity actual value" nodeId="50" actualValue="-22187" defaultValue="0" dataType="0004" kickStatus="1" objectType="7" uniqueIDRef="UID_PARAM_606c" PDOmapping="TPDO" kickUiFormat="updates:r1000; shape:slider; range:-2.14748e+09,2.14748e+09; step:5000"/>
       <CANopenObject accessType="ro" kickStatusTxt="15:42:25 read ok" index="60F4" name="Following error actual value" nodeId="50" actualValue="5" dataType="0004" kickStatus="1" objectType="7" uniqueIDRef="UID_PARAM_60f4" PDOmapping="no" kickUiFormat="updates:r1000; shape:slider; range:-2.14748e+09,2.14748e+09; step:5000"/>
      </CANopenObjectList>
     </EditorObjects>
    </docs>
   </module>
   <module userLevel="2" label="Script" description="MovingCap CODE" panelVisible="0" type="drive_canopen_python"/>
   <properties>
    <NodeId>50</NodeId>
    <ConfigFilePath>MCFLAT_ETH.xdd</ConfigFilePath>
    <ScriptFileName>flattrack_demo.py</ScriptFileName>
    <ScriptHostType>3</ScriptHostType>
    <AccessKeySet/>
    <TargetVelocity>157</TargetVelocity>
    <ScriptDebugMode>0</ScriptDebugMode>
   </properties>
   <slave label="Communication" type="canusb"/>
  </module>
